    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see what you're saying about the \"necessary\" aspect. It's just that some people argue the whole concept of \"progress\" is a flawed way to view it because of the human cost. Do you think it's actually historically accurate to frame those tragedies as a necessary part of building a nation, or is that just one way of looking at it?",
